-- title:
--   Pole-chart unit witness at ∞ on X_H(q²M'), q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ such that some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((\mathsf q))$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange` of `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ that is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ (the units $\equiv 1 \bmod q$). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A\to L$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L\to K$. Let $j\in K$, $j\neq 0$, have Laurent series the coefficient image of the expansion `jq`. Then there is $b\in K$ which is integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$, whose Laurent coefficient in degree $0$ vanishes, and such that for every $L$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $K$ fixing every element of $K$ whose Laurent series lies in the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficient images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-field generated by the expansions $\mathsf{qExpand}\,d\,\mathsf{jq}$ for nonzero divisors $d$ of $q^2M'$, and with $\sigma\neq\mathrm{id}$, the degree-$0$ coefficient of $\sigma b$ lies outside the image of the maximal ideal of $A$ in $L$.
--
--   This is the $q=2$ case of the construction of a function regular on the chart at $\infty$ of a two-chart integral model which vanishes at the cusp $\infty$ while each non-trivial diamond translate has unit constant term; such a function separates $\infty$ from its diamond translates over the residue field of $A$. It feeds the statement that an automorphism fixing the $X_0$-floor and preserving the condition of having constant term in the pole chart is the identity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_mem_chartAlgInf_coeff_zero_eq_zero_forall_algEquiv_coeff_zero_ne_xH_of_eq_two.lean

